meta {
  name: Create Product
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/product
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "Teclado Mecânico RGB",
    "description": "Teclado mecânico com switches blue e iluminação RGB",
    "price": 349.90,
    "category": "Periféricos",
    "imageUrl": "https://example.com/imagens/teclado.jpg"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.body.id) {
    bru.setVar("productId", res.body.id);
  }
  if (res.body.name) {
    bru.setVar("productName", res.body.name);
  }
}

docs {
  Requires auth-service/Login Admin.bru to have run first — needs {{adminAccessToken}}.
  Through "Gateway", POST /api/product requires ROLE_ADMIN
  (JwtAuthenticationFilter.requiresAdmin); through "ProductDirect" (:8082) the header is
  sent but ignored — product-service itself has no Spring Security config yet (see the
  "To DO: @SecurityRequirement / @PreAuthorize" comments in ProductController), so an
  unauthenticated POST against :8082 also succeeds. See
  product-service-errors/Create Product No Token.bru.

  Saves {{productId}} (MongoDB ObjectId) and {{productName}}, used by every
  inventory-service and order-service request below — this is effectively the first
  step of the end-to-end order flow, not just a product-service smoke test.

  Expected: 201 CREATED, Location header /api/product/{id}, body echoes the product
  with its generated id.
}
